{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "A fixed, representative coding-agent memory SESSION for the transport-cost advisory slice (#134 E-D). Eight operations with the concrete per-call request + response payloads on the wire for EACH transport (mcp / cli / rest). Hand-authored to mirror the real tool/route/CLI IO; deterministic.",
    "mix": "3 remember + 2 search + 1 get_facts + 1 revise + 1 resolve = 8 operations.",
    "mixJustification": "Models one working session of a coding agent using 3ngram as memory: it RECORDS more than it READS (writes dominate during active work — capturing decisions/commitments/blockers as they happen), occasionally SEARCHES prior context, checks a current FACT, and CORRECTS one earlier memory (revise) + CLOSES one commitment (resolve). The write-heavy 5:3 write:read ratio reflects an agent mid-task laying down memory, not a read-only recall session. The mix is intentionally small and concrete so totals are auditable by hand.",
    "wireNote": "Each operation gives the request body/args + response body each transport puts ON THE WIRE. MCP args == REST request body == CLI parsed args (one core, N transports), but the ENVELOPE differs: MCP wraps args in a JSON-RPC tools/call request and the result in a content+structuredContent envelope; REST is a bare JSON body + status; CLI is an argv line in + the SDK's already-shaped JSON out (or human text — JSON modeled here as the agent-parseable default)."
  },
